.nh
.TH "PGMCTL" "1" "Oct 2026" "pgman-proxy" "pgmctl Manual"

.SH NAME
pgmctl-promote - Promote NODE out of a join window whose publisher is lost (abandons writes)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpgmctl promote NODE --accept-data-loss --reason TEXT [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
End a join window whose publisher is lost, by promoting NODE.

.PP
A join window is the state where the cluster's failover record lets only
its publisher promote: every other peer was still cloning when it was
published, so only the publisher holds every write it acknowledged. If
the publisher is gone for good, no survivor ever promotes on its own.

.PP
This command abandons every write the publisher acknowledged that NODE
has not received. It:
.IP "  1." 5
reads the join window from the cluster and prints what is lost;
.IP "  2." 5
asks for the typed cluster name (or --force --cluster NAME);
.IP "  3." 5
records the authorization (POST /v1/promotion-authorization) on the
 node it talks to; any live node works, no leader is needed;
.IP "  4." 5
waits until NODE is primary, unless --no-wait.

.PP
pg-manager refuses unless the publisher has been silent for its policy's
abandon window (60s by default), NODE holds the publisher's database,
and no live peer is ahead of NODE. It fences the publisher, so it cannot
promote when it returns; its abandoned writes can be inspected first.
Unfence it to let it re-clone.

.PP
Outside a join window, use 'pgmctl switchover --target NODE' or
\&'pgmctl failover'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--accept-data-loss\fP[=false]
	Required: accept losing the publisher's unreplicated writes

.PP
\fB--cancel\fP[=false]
	Cancel the pending authorization (the publisher stays fenced)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for promote

.PP
\fB--no-wait\fP[=false]
	Return once the authorization is recorded

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Required: why the publisher is abandoned (recorded)

.PP
\fB--replace\fP[=false]
	Replace a pending authorization

.PP
\fB--ttl\fP=0s
	How long the authorization may wait for NODE to promote (default: the cluster policy, 2m)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--cluster\fP=""
	Expected cluster id; pinned before any cluster-affecting op

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	Path to pgmctl config (overrides $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pgmctl/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB--context\fP=""
	Configured context name

.PP
\fB--endpoint\fP=""
	Single-shot pgman-proxy endpoint override

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	Skip cluster-name confirmation (requires --cluster )

.PP
\fB--insecure-skip-tls-verify\fP[=false]
	Disable TLS verification (warned)

.PP
\fB--insecure-skip-version-check\fP[=false]
	Proceed despite minor / major version skew

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Suppress ANSI escapes unconditionally

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format (table, json, yaml, wide)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--strict\fP[=false]
	Treat WARN as non-zero exit

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	Overall command timeout

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	Increase verbosity (-v / -vv / -vvv)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip single-resource confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pgmctl promote node-a --accept-data-loss --reason "node-c volume lost, INC-1234"
  pgmctl promote --cancel
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpgmctl(1)\fP
